    "result_text": "Done. The test suite is green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Contract (`openapi.yml` \u2192 regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`)**\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and optional `addressLine2` to `OwnerFields`.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list, so a structured-only owner (no flat `address`) still satisfies the contract while `city` stays required. Earlier minimal owners (flat `address`) remain accepted.\n\n**Domain + persistence**\n- `Owner` entity gained `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` fields (`@Column address_line1/address_line2`) with getters/setters; MapStruct auto-maps them both ways, so the response returns `addressLine1`.\n- Added the two columns to all four DB schemas (`hsqldb` is what the tests use).\n\n**Behaviour (`ValidateNewOwner`)**\n- The structured form wins whenever `addressLine1` is non-blank; otherwise the flat `address` is used (backward-compatible).\n- Normalization (`OwnerAddress.normalize`: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE) is applied to whichever address fields are supplied.\n- The flat `address` \u2014 the value every downstream reader uses (household hash, postcode validation, locality all key off the shared `city`/`postcode`, and anything reading the street sees `getAddress()`) \u2014 is composed as normalized `addressLine1`, plus a single space and normalized `addressLine2` only when `addressLine2` is present.\n- The required-field check now tests the composed `address`, so \"valid when it supplies an address in either form, plus city\" holds.\n\n**Update path (`ApplyOwner`)** now also carries `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` so a `PUT` doesn't silently drop them.\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass: structured input normalizes and composes (`addressLine1` and `address` both `\"10 KING STREET\"`), and the flat `address` form still returns 2xx.",
